      "message": "This is a bit hard to understand: do you mean\n\n```\nThe current RT1739 driver code sets the VBUS_OVP threshold to 23V. However, in LV_SRC mode, the OVP should be set to 6V to prevent potential damage to the VIN_LV . Additionally, under certain conditions (FRS condition 0x36 bit7), the OVP should be automatically forced to 6V when LV_SRC is enabled.\n\nTo address this potential damage risk, we need to modify the RT1739 driver to properly set the OVP threshold in LV_SRC mode and ensure the safety of the VIN_LV during operation.\n```\n\nIf yes, could you rephrase the commit message accordingly?",
