      "side": 1,
      "message": "The RT1739 VBUS_OV_SETTING 0x24 bit2:0 is no matter what you EN HV_SNK or LV_SRC the VBUS_OVP will follow setting.\nThen it will cause a problem, while EN LV_SRC VBUS_OVP is still set at 23V.\nThat will cause have a VBUS EOS issue.\nThe 0x36 bit7 LVSW_OVP_6V set\u003d1 that will force VBUS_OVP level to 6V when LV_SRC enable.\nThe 0x36 bit7 LVSW_OVP_6V set\u003d0 that will not force VBUS_OVP level to 6V when LV_SRC enable, just follow VBUS_OV_SETTING 0x24 bit2:0\u0027s setting. \nIt is recommended to set 0x36 bit7 LVSW_OVP_6V set to 1.",
